-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 6 (Graduated Retirement Benefit): regulations 15 to 20.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- Parent-law figures taken as stated inputs, never guessed (they are not among the inputs):
--   * the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit (regulation 16(5): from the graduated contributions the
--     deceased paid, under the 1965 Act and the up-rating orders), and the deceased's increase in graduated retirement
--     benefit (regulation 20(5): section 36(4) of the 1965 Act);
--   * the amount of a lump sum under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit)
--     Regulations 2005 (regulation 19(1));
--   * whether the survivor "is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act" (regulation 18(8)), and the
--     rates of the other state pensions the survivor receives under sections 2, 4, 7 and 12 of the 2014 Act (regulation 17);
--   * whether the Secretary of State "considers it reasonable" to allow a late choice (regulation 18(4)(a)): a fact about an
--     official's judgment, asked of the survivor, never presumed.
-- The "6th April 2016" of regulations 15, 16 is the same date as the one regulation 1(3) names and the one the Regulations come
-- into force on (fork F17), so it is the one value `the date the Regulations come into force`.

§ `Part 6 -- Graduated Retirement Benefit`

§§ `Regulation 15: a survivor's state pension based on inheritance of graduated retirement benefit`

-- src:151 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
@ref Regulation 15(2)(a) (src:151)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the survivor has reached pensionable age` `the survivor` MEANS
    Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age`) AT MOST Day (`the survivor`'s `the date as at which the question is asked`)

-- src:153 | (c) the marriage took place, or the civil partnership was formed, before 6th April 2016; and
@ref Regulation 15(2)(c) (src:153)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the marriage or civil partnership began before 6 April 2016` `the survivor` MEANS
    Day (`the survivor`'s `the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed on`) LESS THAN Day `the date the Regulations come into force`

§§ `Regulation 16: the inherited amount`

-- "Under" and "over" pensionable age when the deceased died: the survivor was under it if the death came before the day the
-- survivor reached it, and over it if the death came on or after that day (fork F14: otherwise the day of reaching it would
-- fall in neither limb).
-- src:160 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:164 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
@ref Regulation 16(1)(b), 16(2)(b) (src:160); regulation 16(2)(b) (src:164)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the survivor was under pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor` MEANS
    Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the deceased died`) LESS THAN Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age`)

-- src:168 | (b) they were over pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died.
@ref Regulation 16(3)(b) (src:168)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the survivor was over pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor` MEANS
    Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the deceased died`) AT LEAST Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age`)

-- src:159 | (a) their spouse or civil partner died before 6th April 2016;
@ref Regulation 16(1)(a) (src:159)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deceased died before 6 April 2016` `the survivor` MEANS
    Day (`the survivor`'s `the date the deceased died`) LESS THAN Day `the date the Regulations come into force`

-- "reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016".
-- src:163 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016;
-- src:167 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016; and
@ref Regulation 16(2)(a), 16(3)(a) (src:163); regulation 16(3)(a) (src:167)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deceased reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it` `the survivor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the survivor`'s `the date the deceased reached pensionable age`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `a date` THEN
            Day `a date` LESS THAN Day `the date the Regulations come into force`
        AND NOT (`the deceased died before 6 April 2016` `the survivor`)

-- src:158 | (1) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:159 | (a) their spouse or civil partner died before 6th April 2016;
-- src:160 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:161 | (c) they have not married or formed a civil partnership after the death and before the time they reach pensionable age.
@ref Regulation 16(1) (src:158-161)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(1) applies` `the survivor` MEANS
        `the deceased died before 6 April 2016` `the survivor`
    AND `the survivor was under pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor`
    AND (NOT `the survivor`'s `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age`)

-- src:162 | (2) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:163 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016;
-- src:164 | (b) they were under pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:165 | (c) they have not married or formed a civil partnership after the death and before the time they reach pensionable age.
@ref Regulation 16(2) (src:162-165)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(2) applies` `the survivor` MEANS
        `the deceased reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it` `the survivor`
    AND `the survivor was under pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor`
    AND (NOT `the survivor`'s `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age`)

-- src:166 | (3) For the purposes of regulation 15(2)(d), a person is entitled to an inherited amount if—
-- src:167 | (a) their spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age before 6th April 2016 but died on or after 6th April 2016; and
-- src:168 | (b) they were over pensionable age when their spouse or civil partner died.
@ref Regulation 16(3) (src:166-168)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 16(3) applies` `the survivor` MEANS
        `the deceased reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 but died on or after it` `the survivor`
    AND `the survivor was over pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor`

-- The three paragraphs cannot overlap: (1) needs a death before 6 April 2016 and (2) and (3) a death on or after it, and (2)
-- and (3) need the survivor under and over pensionable age respectively.
@ref Regulation 15(2)(d) (src:154); regulation 16(1), 16(2), 16(3) (src:158-168)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A `Paragraph of regulation 16 a survivor falls within`
`the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` `the survivor` MEANS
    IF   `regulation 16(1) applies` `the survivor`
    THEN `regulation 16(1)`
    ELSE IF   `regulation 16(2) applies` `the survivor`
         THEN `regulation 16(2)`
         ELSE IF   `regulation 16(3) applies` `the survivor`
              THEN `regulation 16(3)`
              ELSE `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`

-- src:179 | (6) The date mentioned in paragraph (4) is—
