    THEN JUST (`the survivor`'s `the date the deceased died`)
    ELSE IF   `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` `the survivor` EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`the survivor`'s `the date the survivor reached or reaches pensionable age`)

-- Paragraph (5): the weekly rate is taken from the graduated contributions, with up-rating orders since the death treated as in
-- force before it and without the additions under section 36(4) or 37(1) of the 1965 Act. That figure is the stated input.
-- src:169 | (4) The inherited amount is half of the weekly rate of the deceased spouse’s or civil partner’s graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with paragraph (5), on the date referred to in paragraph (6) (whether or not the deceased was receiving, or entitled to receive, any such benefit).
-- src:170 | (5) The determination for the purposes of paragraph (4) is carried out by—
-- src:171 | (a) taking the weekly rate of graduated retirement benefit appropriate to the amount of graduated contributions paid by the deceased;
-- src:172 | (b) determining that weekly rate as if any provisions in orders under section 150 of the Administration Act (annual up-rating of benefits) which—
-- src:173 | (i) increase that weekly rate; and
-- src:174 | (ii) have come into force since the date of the deceased’s death,
-- src:175 | had come into force before that date; and
-- src:176 | (c) excluding any addition under—
-- src:177 | (i) section 36(4) of the 1965 Act; or
-- src:178 | (ii) section 37(1) of that Act.
@ref Regulation 16(4), 16(5) (src:169-178)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
