GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the inherited amount` `the survivor` `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined as paragraph (5) requires` MEANS
    IF   `the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` `the survivor` EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined as paragraph (5) requires` / 2)

§§ `Regulation 15 continued: entitlement and rate`

-- src:149 | (1) A person whose dead spouse or civil partner paid graduated contributions as an insured person is entitled to a state pension in accordance with this regulation.
-- src:150 | (2) Such a person is entitled to a state pension if—
-- src:151 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:152 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:153 | (c) the marriage took place, or the civil partnership was formed, before 6th April 2016; and
-- src:154 | (d) that person is entitled to an inherited amount under regulation 16(1), (2) or (3).
@ref Regulation 15(1), 15(2) (src:149-154)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a state pension is payable under regulation 15` `the survivor` MEANS
        `the survivor`'s `the deceased paid graduated contributions as an insured person`
    AND `the survivor has reached pensionable age` `the survivor`
    AND `the survivor`'s `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died`
    AND `the marriage or civil partnership began before 6 April 2016` `the survivor`
    AND NOT (`the paragraph of regulation 16 the survivor falls within` `the survivor` EQUALS `none of regulation 16(1), (2) or (3)`)

-- src:155 | (3) A state pension under this regulation is payable at a weekly rate equal to the inherited amount determined in accordance with regulation 16(4) to (6).
@ref Regulation 15(3) (src:155)
GIVEN `the survivor` IS A `Facts about a survivor`
      `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined as paragraph (5) requires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly rate of a state pension under regulation 15` `the survivor` `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined as paragraph (5) requires` MEANS
    IF   `a state pension is payable under regulation 15` `the survivor`
    THEN `the inherited amount` `the survivor` `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined as paragraph (5) requires`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 17: up-rating`

-- The three cases partition the position: the other pensions alone reach the full rate (paragraph (8)); they fall short of it and
-- the survivor's pension on top does not exceed it (paragraph (3)); or they fall short of it and the pension takes the total over
-- it (paragraph (5)). Whether anything rises depends then on which event happens: a rise in the full rate, an uprating order.
-- src:189 | (a) that rate, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act (entitlement to state pension at various rates), is equal to or less than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:196 | (i) that rate, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, exceeds the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:197 | (ii) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is less than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:208 | (a) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is equal to or higher than the full rate of the state pension; and
@ref Regulation 17(3)(a), 17(5)(a), 17(8)(a) (src:189); regulation 17(5)(a) (src:196-197); regulation 17(8)(a) (src:208)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
GIVETH A `Which up-rating case of regulation 17 applies`
`the up-rating case that applies` `the facts` MEANS
    IF   `the facts`'s `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act` AT LEAST `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase`
    THEN `regulation 17(8) and (9): the pension rises by the percentage in the uprating order`
    ELSE IF   `the facts`'s `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` PLUS `the facts`'s `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act` AT MOST `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase`
         THEN `regulation 17(3) and (4): the pension rises by the same percentage as the full rate`
         ELSE `regulation 17(5) to (7): the pension rises by a percentage of the shortfall, the excess, or both`

-- "increased by the same percentage as the increase in the full rate": a base amount rises by the full rate's proportional rise.
-- src:192 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the same percentage as the increase in the full rate; and
-- src:202 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the shortfall immediately before the full rate of the state pension is increased (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage by which the full rate is increased); and
@ref Regulation 17(4)(a), 17(6)(a) (src:192); regulation 17(6)(a) (src:202)
GIVEN `the base` IS A NUMBER
      `the facts` IS A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rise from an increase in the full rate, applied to a base of` `the base` `given` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension after an increase, if the full rate is increased`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST `the new full rate` THEN
        `the base` TIMES ((`the new full rate` MINUS `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase`) / `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase`)

-- "by the percentage specified in the uprating order" applied to a base amount.
-- src:205 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the excess immediately before the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (5)(b)(ii) comes into force (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage specified in that uprating order); and
-- src:211 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the percentage specified in the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (8)(b); and
@ref Regulation 17(7)(a), 17(9)(a) (src:205); regulation 17(9)(a) (src:211)
GIVEN `the base` IS A NUMBER
      `the facts` IS A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rise from an uprating order, applied to a base of` `the base` `given` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the percentage specified in an uprating order, if one comes into force`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST `the percentage` THEN `the base` TIMES `the percentage`

-- Paragraph (6): the shortfall is the full rate less the other pensions; paragraph (7): the excess is the survivor's pension plus
-- the other pensions less the full rate. If both events happen, each rise is worked from the position immediately before its own
-- event and the two are added (fork F15).
-- src:183 | (1) The rate of a person’s state pension under regulation 15 is to be increased as follows.
-- src:191 | (4) Where paragraph (3) applies—
-- src:192 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the same percentage as the increase in the full rate; and
-- src:193 | (b) that increase of the person’s state pension is to be made at the same time as the increase in the full rate.
-- src:194 | (5) The rate of the person’s state pension is increased in accordance with either or both of paragraphs (6) and (7) where—
-- src:195 | (a) both—
-- src:196 | (i) that rate, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, exceeds the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:197 | (ii) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is less than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:198 | (b) either or both of the following occurs at any time—
-- src:199 | (i) the full rate of the state pension is increased;
-- src:200 | (ii) an uprating order comes into force.
-- src:201 | (6) Where paragraph (5)(a) and (b)(i) applies, the rate of the person’s state pension is increased—
-- src:202 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the shortfall immediately before the full rate of the state pension is increased (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage by which the full rate is increased); and
-- src:203 | (b) at the same time as paragraph (5)(b)(i) applies.
-- src:204 | (7) Where paragraph (5)(a) and (b)(ii) applies, the rate of the person’s state pension is increased—
-- src:205 | (a) by an amount equal to the appropriate percentage of the excess immediately before the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (5)(b)(ii) comes into force (“the appropriate percentage” means the percentage specified in that uprating order); and
-- src:206 | (b) at the same time as that uprating order comes into force.
-- src:207 | (8) The rate of the person’s state pension is increased in accordance with paragraph (9) where—
-- src:208 | (a) the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act is equal to or higher than the full rate of the state pension; and
-- src:209 | (b) an uprating order comes into force at any time.
-- src:210 | (9) Where paragraph (8) applies—
-- src:211 | (a) the rate of the person’s state pension is increased by the percentage specified in the uprating order mentioned in paragraph (8)(b); and
-- src:212 | (b) that increase of the person’s state pension is to be made at the same time as that uprating order comes into force.
-- src:213 | (10) In this regulation—
-- src:214 | “the excess” means the amount by which the rate of the state pension, when added to the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, exceeds the full rate;
-- src:215 | “the shortfall” means the amount by which the sum of the rate of any state pension to which the person is entitled under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act, is less than the full rate;
-- src:216 | “uprating order” means an order under section 151A of the Administration Act (up-rating of transitional state pensions under the 2014 Act).
@ref Regulation 17(1) (src:183); regulation 17(4), 17(6), 17(7), 17(9), 17(10) (src:191-216)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the up-rating case that applies` `the facts`
    WHEN `regulation 17(3) and (4): the pension rises by the same percentage as the full rate` THEN
        `the rise from an increase in the full rate, applied to a base of` (`the facts`'s `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15`) `given` `the facts`
    WHEN `regulation 17(5) to (7): the pension rises by a percentage of the shortfall, the excess, or both` THEN
        `the rise from an increase in the full rate, applied to a base of` (`the shortfall`) `given` `the facts`
        PLUS `the rise from an uprating order, applied to a base of` (`the excess`) `given` `the facts`
    WHEN `regulation 17(8) and (9): the pension rises by the percentage in the uprating order` THEN
        `the rise from an uprating order, applied to a base of` (`the facts`'s `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15`) `given` `the facts`
    WHERE
        `the shortfall` MEANS `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase` MINUS `the facts`'s `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act`
        `the excess` MEANS (`the facts`'s `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` PLUS `the facts`'s `the sum of the rates of any state pension the person is entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act`) MINUS `the facts`'s `the full rate of the state pension immediately before any increase`

-- src:156 | (4) The rate of the state pension for a person under this regulation is to be increased from time to time in accordance with regulation 17.
@ref Regulation 15(4) (src:156)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for the up-rating of a survivor's state pension`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15 after the increase` `the facts` MEANS
    `the facts`'s `the rate of the person's state pension under regulation 15` PLUS `the increase in the rate of the person's state pension` `the facts`

§§ `Regulation 18: choosing a lump sum or a state pension`

-- src:219 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:220 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:221 | (c) the spouse’s or civil partner’s entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death; and
