GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conditions of regulation 18(1)(a) to (d) are met` `the survivor` MEANS
        `the survivor has reached pensionable age` `the survivor`
    AND `the survivor`'s `the survivor and the deceased were married or civil partners of each other when the deceased died`
    AND `the survivor`'s `the deceased's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death and throughout the 12 months ending with the day before the death`
    AND (    (    `the survivor was under pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor`
              AND (NOT `the survivor`'s `the survivor has married or formed a civil partnership since the death and before reaching pensionable age`))
         OR  `the survivor was over pensionable age when the deceased died` `the survivor`)

-- src:218 | (1) Subject to paragraph (8), a person is entitled to a choice under this regulation if—
