@ref Regulation 18(5), 18(11) (src:234); regulation 18(11) (src:247)
GIVEN `the period has ended without a choice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What is paid under regulation 18`
`what is paid where no choice has been made` `the period has ended without a choice` MEANS
    IF   `the period has ended without a choice`
    THEN `a lump sum under regulation 19`
    ELSE `nothing yet, because the person can still make a choice`

-- Paragraph (3): a choice not made in the manner of regulation 5(2) and (3) is no choice. Paragraph (4): the period is
-- regulation 4(2) and (3), and a late choice is allowed on the conditions of (4)(a) and (b). Paragraph (5): a late choice that is
-- not allowed leaves the person with the lump sum. Paragraph (6): a late choice for a state pension reduces the lump sum to nil,
-- which is the outcome "a state pension" and no lump sum.
