§§ `Regulation 20: a state pension based on inheritance of deferred graduated retirement benefit`

-- Sub-paragraphs (e) and (f) bite only on the two kinds of person they name: one entitled to a choice under regulation 18 must have
-- chosen a state pension; one who would be but for regulation 18(8) must be so paid by virtue of 18(9)(b) or (10)(b). Anyone else
-- (the deceased was entitled to an increase) passes both. Both come to: the person is paid a state pension under regulation 20.
-- src:252 | (1) A person is entitled to a state pension under this regulation if—
-- src:253 | (a) that person has reached pensionable age;
-- src:254 | (b) that person’s spouse died while they were married or that person’s civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other;
-- src:255 | (c) either—
-- src:256 | (i) that person was under pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died and did not marry or form a civil partnership between the date of death and the date that person reached pensionable age; or
-- src:257 | (ii) that person was over pensionable age when the spouse or civil partner died;
-- src:258 | (d) either—
-- src:259 | (i) that person’s spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit; or
-- src:260 | (ii) that person’s spouse’s or civil partner’s entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when the spouse or civil partner died;
-- src:261 | (e) in the case of a person entitled to a choice under regulation 18, that person has chosen to be paid a state pension under this regulation; and
-- src:262 | (f) in the case of a person who is not entitled to a choice under regulation 18 because regulation 18(8) applies to them, that person is to be paid a state pension under this regulation by virtue of regulation 18(9)(b) or (10)(b).
